1
00:00:01,090 --> 00:00:07,960
This is a government claims service. No
WebMCP, no agent hooks — just well marked
up HTML.

2
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:14,200
Reflex reads the page and proposes tools.
Nothing is registered until a human
approves it.

3
00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:20,740
Two read-only capabilities, approved. They
are now real WebMCP tools on this page.

4
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:28,920
An agent calls search claims with a
claimant's name. The service's own form is
filled and submitted. Driven, not

5
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:33,780
The claim comes back, and the tool returns
the text the page then showed.

6
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:43,080
Destructive tools are different. Reflex
asks a human, in the page, on every single
call.

7
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:47,310
Dismissed, so nothing happened. The claim
is untouched.
